10.text:
The residual light-dependent Cy5 signal with the second (CH2OH) probe is produced solely by continued action of the unchanged thioxanthenone photosensitizer (A). It remains the only 417 nm absorber present in both experiments and, once the phenolic OH is removed, can still drive lower-yield direct HAT, energy transfer or ROS chemistry on the bicyclo[4.2.0] core or benzylic CH2OH site, yielding attenuated but detectable covalent alkyne attachment that survives click.  

B is eliminated by the structural swap itself (no phenolic OH remains). C cannot explain the graded attenuation: any retro-[2+2] opening to the Michael-acceptor enoate would be independent of the remote phenyl substituent and should therefore give comparable labeling intensity for both probes, yet the data show a sharp drop. D lacks any mechanistic or structural basis under the stated conditions, and E is added after irradiation and therefore cannot create light dependence. The observed pattern (strong → weak residual light-vs-dark difference) is therefore fully accounted for only by residual sensitization from A.  

PUBLIC RESPONSE: {A}

